Package: caboose-computer-use
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Braedon Saunders <bsaunders@rassaun.com>
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Depends: nodejs (>= 18), python3 (>= 3.11), python3-gi, gir1.2-atspi-2.0, gir1.2-glib-2.0, gir1.2-gdkpixbuf-2.0, at-spi2-core, libglib2.0-bin, libx11-6, libxres1, x11-utils, xdotool, imagemagick, tesseract-ocr, tesseract-ocr-eng, sudo
Recommends: chromium, python3-uno, libatk-wrapper-java-jni, flatpak
Suggests: caboose-computer-use-wine
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Homepage: https://github.com/braedonsaunders/caboose
Description: Caboose computer use: agents drive applications on their own seat
 An MCP server (caboose-computer-use, stdio) with three tools, look, act and
 screenshot, that read and operate the applications on the computer's agent seat
 through their accessibility trees, typed direct tools (D-Bus actions, GSettings,
 LibreOffice UNO, MPRIS, the portal file chooser, files in the agent's home) and
 page tools (WebMCP), with OCR for what an application leaves out of its tree.
 Also the agent seat's start (/usr/libexec/caboose/agent-seat) and profile
 (/usr/libexec/caboose/agent-profile) entry points, and the touch targets the
 phone aims with.
